{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5qcoys3hkNqVpNhUUf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the DurationField error message. One existing test now fails, but that's expected: it checks for the old, wrong text.\n\n**The change:** in `django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1590`, the format shown in the `invalid` error message is now `[DD] [[HH:]MM:]ss[.uuuuuu]`. It used to say `[DD] [HH:[MM:]]ss[.uuuuuu]`. The new version matches how input is actually read: seconds are required, minutes are optional, and hours can only be given along with minutes. So `14:00` means 14 minutes.\n\n**Tests:** I ran the `model_fields` tests: 261 ran, 48 were skipped, and 1 failed. The failure is `test_invalid_string` in `tests/model_fields/test_durationfield.py:78`, which expects the old message word for word. I didn't touch it because the rules say not to edit test files. It should pass once that test's expected string is updated to the new format.\n\n**Not done:**\n- The translation files under `django/conf/locale/` still contain the old message ID. Normally those get regenerated as part of the translation process rather than edited by hand.\n- I didn't add the default `help_text` the issue also suggests. That would be a new feature, and the request was for the smallest fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":141,"cache_read_input_tokens":19608,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":141},"output_tokens":418,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9252005b-909d-479e-8581-ff0a839a65d4","uuid":"6970f5c8-0ff9-4e73-8976-ded938979daf","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:38:33.849Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5qcg3a1rS4yT7RPivv"}
